{"command": "cat > /testbed/.specify/memory/constitution.md << 'CONSTITUTION_EOF'\n<!-- SYNC IMPACT REPORT\nVersion change: 0.0.0 → 1.0.0\nModified principles: None (first version)\nAdded sections: Core Principles (I–V), Governance\nRemoved sections: None\nDeferred items: None\n-->\n# TinyDB Constitution\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### I. Preserve Existing Public API Behavior\nAll changes to TinyDB MUST maintain backward compatibility with the existing public API. The public surface includes `TinyDB`, `Storage`, `JSONStorage`, `Query`, and `where`. Any modification that alters documented behavior, method signatures, or return types requires a MAJOR version bump and explicit migration guidance. No undocumented behavior changes are permitted in MINOR or PATCH releases.\n\n### II. Attach Testable Acceptance Criteria to Requirements\nEvery requirement, feature, or bug fix MUST have corresponding testable acceptance criteria. Acceptance criteria must be expressed as concrete, executable tests that verify the expected behavior. Requirements without associated tests are considered incomplete and must not be merged.\n\n### III. Distinguish Observed Evidence from Unverified Assertions\nClaims about system behavior, performance, or correctness MUST be supported by observed evidence—test results, benchmarks, or reproducible logs. Unverified assertions, including assumptions about edge cases or user expectations, must be explicitly flagged as such and validated before being treated as fact.\n\n### IV. Prefer Simple Scoped Implementations\nImplementations MUST favor simplicity and narrow scope. Each change should address a single concern with minimal complexity. Avoid over-engineering, premature abstraction, or features that extend beyond the stated requirement. When in doubt, choose the simpler solution and justify any added complexity.\n\n### V. Document Unresolved Assumptions and Regressions\nAny unresolved assumptions, known limitations, or potential regressions MUST be documented alongside the code change. Documentation includes inline comments, docstrings, or a dedicated tracking section. Undocumented assumptions are treated as defects and must be resolved or explicitly acknowledged before merging.\n\n## Governance\n\nAll development work on TinyDB MUST comply with these principles. Amendments to this constitution require:\n\n1. A clear description of the proposed change and its rationale.\n2. Impact assessment on existing public API and test coverage.\n3. Version bump per semantic versioning (MAJOR for principle removals/redefinitions, MINOR for new principles, PATCH for clarifications).\n4. Updated ratification and last-amended dates.\n\nCompliance is verified through code review and test execution. Complexity must be justified; simplicity is the default.\n\n**Version**: 1.0.0 | **Ratified**: 2026-09-17 | **Last Amended**: 2026-09-17\nCONSTITUTION_EOF", "exit_code": 0, "stderr": "", "stdout": ""}